{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y_safestan_observed`, a deterministic tail copy of the originally scored observations `y[3:T]`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added `y_safestan_observed` with deterministic relation `y_safestan_observed[i] = y[i + 2]` for `i = 1, ..., T - 2`, because the original model sampled indexed elements `y[t]` inside a loop. SafeStan requires protected data to be a top-level identifier sampled exactly once outside loops. The scalar likelihood loop was replaced by an equivalent vectorized normal sampling statement using a local `y_hat` vector computed after the parameter priors. The original `y` remains context data for the moving-average residual recursion; no new observations were introduced and the posterior/log density is preserved for data satisfying the documented copy relation.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=3> T; // number of observations
  vector[T] y; // observation at time T
  vector[T - 2] y_safestan_observed; // deterministic copy of y[3:T]
}
parameters {
  real mu; // mean
  real<lower=0> sigma; // error scale
  vector[2] theta; // lag coefficients
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[T] epsilon; // error terms
  epsilon[1] = y[1] - mu;
  epsilon[2] = y[2] - mu - theta[1] * epsilon[1];
  for (t in 3 : T) {
    epsilon[t] = y[t] - mu - theta[1] * epsilon[t - 1]
                 - theta[2] * epsilon[t - 2];
  }
}
model {
  vector[T - 2] y_hat;

  mu ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  theta ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);
  sigma ~ cauchy(0, 2.5);

  for (t in 3 : T) {
    y_hat[t - 2] = mu + theta[1] * epsilon[t - 1]
                   + theta[2] * epsilon[t - 2];
  }
  y_safestan_observed ~ normal(y_hat, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"T":4,"y":[5.267813142169018,6.3220402224317676,4.91165552081635,5.100083697034425],"y_safestan_observed":[4.91165552081635,5.100083697034425]}","protected_variables":["y_safestan_observed"]}
